    "question": "Ajax is 80 kilograms. He is planning to lose some weight. Exercising for an hour will help him lose 1.5 pounds. If 1 kilogram is equal to 2.2 pounds How many pounds will he weigh if he exercises for 2 hours every day for two weeks?",
    "gold": "134",
    "answer": "Ajax weighs 80 x 2.2 = <<80*2.2=176>>176 in pounds.\nHe will lose 1.5 x 2 = <<1.5*2=3>>3 pounds per day.\nSo he will lose 3 x 7 = <<3*7=21>>21 pounds per week.\nSo, he will lose 21x 2 = <<21*2=42>>42 pounds after 2 weeks.\nTherefore, he will weigh 176 - 42 = <<176-42=134>>134 pounds after 2 weeks.\n#### 134"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much weight Ajax will lose and his final weight after exercising for 2 hours every day for two weeks, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert Ajax's weight from kilograms to pounds:**\n   Ajax's weight is 80 kilograms. Since 1 kilogram is equal to 2.2 pounds, we can convert his weight to pounds as follows:\n   \\[\n   80 \\text{ kg} \\times 2.2 \\text{ pounds/kg} = 176 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total weight loss from exercising:**\n   Ajax exercises for 2 hours every day for two weeks. Since he loses 1.5 pounds per hour of exercise, the total weight loss per day is:\n   \\[\n   2 \\text{ hours/day} \\times 1.5 \\text{ pounds/hour} = 3 \\text{ pounds/day}\n   \\]\n   Over two weeks (14 days), the total weight loss is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ pounds/day} \\times 14 \\text{ days} = 42 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate Ajax's final weight:**\n   Subtract the total weight loss from his initial weight in pounds:\n   \\[\n   176 \\text{ pounds} - 42 \\text{ pounds} = 134 \\text{ pounds}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Ajax's final weight after exercising for 2 hours every day for two weeks is \\(\\boxed{134}\\) pounds.",
